{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775377912-aXRWnKXWjncDRXKJUHCd","role":"assistant","created":1775377926,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the Treasury Bulletin structure, I see there is table FFO-3 with \"On-Budget and Off-Budget Outlays by Agency\" but the data shown is the total. There's also table FFO-4 with more detailed breakdowns by fund type.\n\nBut looking at the question more carefully: \"total on-budget and off-budget outlays\" - I think the question is asking for the combined total outlays (on-budget + off-budget) for the Judicial Branch. That would be the values from the FFO-3 table.\n\nLooking at the Judicial Branch data:\n- FY 2007: 6,008\n- FY 2008: 6,345\n- FY 2009: 6,643\n- FY 2010: 7,185\n- FY 2011: 7,296\n- FY 2012: 7,228 (from 2014 bulletin)\n- FY 2013: 7,066 (from 2014 bulletin)\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Calculate YoY growth rates\n2. Calculate average YoY growth rate\n3. Run OLS regression of ln(outlays) on fiscal year index\n\nLet me do that calculation.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_c6bef39e0bd847ffa1ca32cc","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport math\n\n# Judicial Branch total outlays (millions) from the bulletins\n# Using 2014 bulletin for 2012-2013, and 2011 bulletin for 2007-2011\n# The slight difference in 2011 values (7296 vs 7295) - using 2014 bulletin as more recent\n\ndata = {\n    2007: 6008,\n    2008: 6345,\n    2009: 6643,\n    2010: 7185,\n    2011: 7295,  # using 2014 bulletin value\n    2012: 7228,\n    2013: 7066\n}\n\n# Calculate YoY growth rates\nprint(\"Judicial Branch Total Outlays (millions):\")\nfor year in range(2007, 2014):\n    print(f\"FY {year}: {data[year]}\")\n\nprint(\"\\nYear-over-Year Growth Rates:\")\nyoy_growth = []\nfor year in range(2008, 2014):\n    growth = (data[year] - data[year-1]) / data[year-1] * 100\n    yoy_growth.append(growth)\n    print(f\"FY {year-1} to FY {year}: {growth:.4f}%\")\n\n# Average YoY growth rate\navg_yoy = sum(yoy_growth) / len(yoy_growth)\nprint(f\"\\nAverage YoY Growth Rate: {avg_yoy:.4f}%\")\n\n# Now OLS regression: ln(outlays) on fiscal year index\n# Using fiscal year index as 1, 2, 3, ... for 2007, 2008, ...\nprint(\"\\nOLS Regression of ln(outlays) on fiscal year index:\")\n\n# Prepare data\nX = []  # fiscal year index (1, 2, 3, ...)\ny = []  # ln(outlays)\nfor i, year in enumerate(range(2007, 2014)):\n    X.append(i + 1)  # index: 1 for 2007, 2 for 2008, etc.\n    y.append(math.log(data[year]))\n\nprint(\"Data points:\")\nfor i, year in enumerate(range(2007, 2014)):\n    print(f\"Index {X[i]}: FY {year}, outlays={data[year]}, ln(outlays)={y[i]:.6f}\")\n\n# Calculate OLS manually\nn = len(X)\nsum_x = sum(X)\nsum_y = sum(y)\nsum_xy = sum([X[i]*y[i] for i in range(n)])\nsum_x2 = sum([X[i]**2 for i in range(n)])\n\n# Slope (beta) and Intercept (alpha)\nslope = (n * sum_xy - sum_x * sum_y) / (n * sum_x2 - sum_x**2)\nintercept = (sum_y - slope * sum_x) / n\n\nprint(f\"\\nOLS Results:\")\nprint(f\"Slope: {slope:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"Intercept: {intercept:.6f}\")\n\n# Round outputs as required\n# YoY growth rate: round to nearest hundredths place\navg_yoy_rounded = round(avg_yoy, 2)\nprint(f\"\\nAverage YoY (rounded to 100ths): {avg_yoy_rounded}\")\n\n# OLS slope and intercept: round to nearest thousandths\nslope_rounded = round(slope, 3)\nintercept_rounded = round(intercept, 3)\nprint(f\"Slope (rounded to 1000ths): {slope_rounded}\")\nprint(f\"Intercept (rounded to 1000ths): {intercept_rounded}\")\n\n# Final output format: [YoY%, slope, intercept]\nprint(f\"\\nFinal Answer: [{avg_yoy_rounded}, {slope_rounded}, {intercept_rounded}]\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
