l places (hundredths)\n\n\n- OLS: 3 decimal places (thousandths)\n\nBut then adds \"All numbers should be rounded to the nearest thousandth place\" - this could be a clarifying statement or could override.\n\nGiven the ambiguity, I'll interpret \"All numbers should be rounded to the nearest thousandth place\" as the final instruction that applies to all numbers. That's [2.806, 0.03, 8.706].\n\nI'm sticking with 3 decimal places for all three values as the most consistent interpretation of the final instruction.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_4f2dea49789544b0af59eca7","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Looking at the table data from the bulletins more carefully\n# The table is titled \"On-Budget and Off-Budget Outlays by Agency\"\n# The values in the Judicial branch column represent the TOTAL outlays (combined)\n\n# Let me verify by checking what the \"Total funds\" column means in the other table \n# and confirm these match\n\n# From 2011 bulletin page 23 - extracting FY 2007-2011 judicial branch\n# From 2014 bulletin page 22 - extracting FY 2010-2013 judicial branch\n\n# Using both sources:\n# FY 2007: 6008 (from 2011)\n# FY 2008: 6345 (from 2011)\n# FY 2009: 6643 (from 2011)\n# FY 2010: 7185 (from both)\n# FY 2011: 7295 (from 2014, slightly different from 2011's 7296)\n# FY 2012: 7228 (from 2014)\n# FY 2013: 7066 (from 2014)\n\n# These are already the combined on-budget + off-budget totals\n\ndata = {\n    2007: 6008,\n    2008: 6345,\n    2009: 6643,\n    2010: 7185,\n    2011: 7295,\n    2012: 7228,\n    2013: 7066\n}\n\n# Verify the combined interpretation is correct by checking a few values in the text\n# The table in the bulletin shows a single value for Judicial Branch per year\n# which represents the total outlays for that agency\n\nprint(\"Data is ready. Final calculation:\")\n\nimport math\n\n# Calculate YoY growth rates\nyoy_growth = []\nfor year in range(2008, 2014):\n    growth = (data[year] - data[year-1]) / data[year-1] * 100\n    yoy_growth.append(growth)\n\navg_yoy = sum(yoy_growth) / len(yoy_growth)\n\n# OLS regression\nX = []\ny = []\nfor i, year in enumerate(range(2007, 2014)):\n    X.append(i + 1)\n    y.append(math.log(data[year]))\n\nn = len(X)\nsum_x = sum(X)\nsum_y = sum(y)\nsum_xy = sum([X[i]*y[i] for i in range(n)])\nsum_x2 = sum([X[i]**2 for i in range(n)])\n\nslope = (n * sum_xy - sum_x * sum_y) / (n * sum_x2 - sum_x**2)\nintercept = (sum_y - slope * sum_x) / n\n\n# Round all to thousandths (3 decimal places) as per final instruction\navg_yoy_rounded = round(avg_yoy, 3)\nslope_rounded = round(slope, 3)\nintercept_rounded = round(intercept, 3)\n\nprint(f\"YoY Growth Rate (avg): {avg_yoy_rounded}%\")\nprint(f\"OLS Slope: {slope_rounded}\")\nprint(f\"OLS Intercept: {intercept_rounded}\")\nprint(f\"\\nFinal Answer: [{avg_yoy_rounded}, {slope_rounded}, {intercept_rounded}]\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
